From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WiVRn Android port <noreply@invalid>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] aux/vk: fix two real Vulkan validation findings in
 vk_create_image_from_native

Both caught live via Vulkan validation while getting real validation
working for the first time on the Android port's server-app
(wivrn-android's docs/ANDROID_PORT.md, HEVC A/B diagnostic milestone):

1. vkGetImageMemoryRequirements() was called unconditionally on the
   freshly-created image, even for AHardwareBuffer-imported images --
   invalid per VUID-vkGetImageMemoryRequirements-image-04004 (must be
   bound to memory first for that handle type), and the result was
   discarded anyway since the AHARDWAREBUFFER branch right below
   overwrites requirements.size/memoryTypeBits from
   vkGetAndroidHardwareBufferPropertiesANDROID. Skip the call for that
   handle type, matching vk_image_allocator.c's create_image(), which
   already does this correctly for its own (allocate rather than
   import) path.

2. When downgrading VK_FORMAT_R8G8B8A8_SRGB to _UNORM for AHardwareBuffer
   import compatibility, the image was not created with
   VK_IMAGE_CREATE_MUTABLE_FORMAT_BIT -- required by
   VUID-VkImageViewCreateInfo-image-01019 whenever an image view's format
   differs from the image's own format. create_image() (the allocating
   counterpart in vk_image_allocator.c) already sets this flag correctly
   when doing the identical downgrade; this path did not.
---
 src/xrt/auxiliary/vk/vk_helpers.c | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/xrt/auxiliary/vk/vk_helpers.c b/src/xrt/auxiliary/vk/vk_helpers.c
index 023b8dd89..44d1b2d1c 100644
--- a/src/xrt/auxiliary/vk/vk_helpers.c
+++ b/src/xrt/auxiliary/vk/vk_helpers.c
@@ -367,6 +367,8 @@ vk_create_image_from_native(struct vk_bundle *vk,
 	// This is the format we allocate the image in, can be changed further down.
 	VkFormat image_format = (VkFormat)info->format;
 
+	bool force_mutable_for_srgb_downgrade = false;
+
 #ifdef XRT_GRAPHICS_BUFFER_HANDLE_IS_AHARDWAREBUFFER
 	/*
 	 * Some Vulkan drivers will natively support importing and exporting
@@ -375,11 +377,16 @@ vk_create_image_from_native(struct vk_bundle *vk,
 	 * While others (arm Mali) does not support importing and exporting
 	 * sRGB formats. So we need to create the image without sRGB and
 	 * then create the image views with sRGB which is allowed by the
-	 * Vulkan spec. It seems to be safe to do with on all drivers,
-	 * so to reduce the logic do that instead.
+	 * Vulkan spec -- but only if VK_IMAGE_CREATE_MUTABLE_FORMAT_BIT was
+	 * set on the image at creation time (VUID-VkImageViewCreateInfo-image-01019),
+	 * which this path was not doing (caught live by Vulkan validation:
+	 * "Formats must be identical unless VK_IMAGE_CREATE_MUTABLE_FORMAT_BIT
+	 * was set on image creation"). It seems to be safe to do with on all
+	 * drivers, so to reduce the logic do that instead.
 	 */
 	if (image_format == VK_FORMAT_R8G8B8A8_SRGB) {
 		image_format = VK_FORMAT_R8G8B8A8_UNORM;
+		force_mutable_for_srgb_downgrade = true;
 	}
 #endif
 
@@ -403,8 +410,10 @@ vk_create_image_from_native(struct vk_bundle *vk,
 	}
 
 	VkImageCreateFlags image_create_flags = 0;
-	// Set the image create mutable flag if usage mutable is given.
-	const bool has_mutable_usage = (info->bits & XRT_SWAPCHAIN_USAGE_MUTABLE_FORMAT) != 0;
+	// Set the image create mutable flag if usage mutable is given, or if
+	// the sRGB->UNORM downgrade above needs it.
+	const bool has_mutable_usage =
+	    ((info->bits & XRT_SWAPCHAIN_USAGE_MUTABLE_FORMAT) != 0) || force_mutable_for_srgb_downgrade;
 	if (has_mutable_usage) {
 		image_create_flags |= VK_IMAGE_CREATE_MUTABLE_FORMAT_BIT;
 	}
@@ -464,7 +473,17 @@ vk_create_image_from_native(struct vk_bundle *vk,
 	}
 
 	VkMemoryRequirements requirements = {0};
+#if !defined(XRT_GRAPHICS_BUFFER_HANDLE_IS_AHARDWAREBUFFER)
+	// For AHardwareBuffer handles this queries requirements on an image
+	// that isn't bound to memory yet (VUID-vkGetImageMemoryRequirements-image-04004,
+	// caught live by Vulkan validation), and the AHARDWAREBUFFER branch
+	// below overwrites requirements.size/memoryTypeBits from
+	// vkGetAndroidHardwareBufferPropertiesANDROID anyway -- this call's
+	// result was unused in that case. Matches vk_image_allocator.c's
+	// create_image(), which already skips the equivalent call for the
+	// same reason.
 	vk->vkGetImageMemoryRequirements(vk->device, image, &requirements);
+#endif
 
 #if defined(XRT_GRAPHICS_BUFFER_HANDLE_IS_FD)
 	VkImportMemoryFdInfoKHR import_memory_info = {
